You really are quite the master of this particular kind of motion panning. This one stood out to me less for the freezing of the moment than for the way it has that AND still has enough "imperfect" motion blur in the water splashes and subject himself to convey the utter chaos of the watersport. Just awesome action photography, generally.</td>', 'You really are quite the master of this particular kind of motion panning. This one stood out to me less for the freezing of the moment than for the way it has that AND still has enough "imperfect" motion blur in the water splashes and subject himself to convey the utter chaos of the watersport. Just awesome action photography, generally.', '2026-08-12 13:00:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(7832970, 1311337, 12200, '<td valign="top">
<table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by tanguera:</b></div><hr/><i> Unfair advantage to have a willing child... ;)</i></td></tr></table>
<br/>
<br/>I''m inclined to agree. All three of my kids tend to be willing--in spurts--and I try never to take that for granted. I just hope one day they look back at some of these and are glad they got to be a part of it all. My only rule is to let them have final say in whether or not I have their okay to use a capture. Nora looked at this one and seemed to like it, but she said, "I look like a ghost."
<br/>
<br/>Thanks, everyone, for the amazing comments and warmer-than-expected reception for this image!</td>', 'Originally posted by tanguera: Unfair advantage to have a willing child... ;)

I''m inclined to agree. All three of my kids tend to be willing--in spurts--and I try never to take that for granted. I just hope one day they look back at some of these and are glad they got to be a part of it all. My only rule is to let them have final say in whether or not I have their okay to use a capture. Nora looked at this one and seemed to like it, but she said, "I look like a ghost."

Thanks, everyone, for the amazing comments and warmer-than-expected reception for this image!', '2026-08-12 13:05:43.000000', NULL, 0),
